3. REMOVED FROM THE UPSTREAM WORK
---------------------------------

The upstream repository carried this carve-out in its README:

    "Files in the players/ directory are copyrighted by their respective
     owners and are included here for reference/attribution purposes only.
     All rights remain with their respective copyright holders."

Those files were the faces of the four AI rivals. Copilot, Hubot and Mona are
GitHub mascots; the artwork was not licensed for redistribution under MIT.

The entire players/ directory has therefore been deleted from this project:

    players/copilot.png       players/car_copilot.png
    players/frank.png         players/car_frank.png
    players/hubot.png         players/car_hubot.png
    players/mona.png          players/car_mona.png

Also removed: the GitHub Octocat sticker that the DESK CHAOS track drew
procedurally onto its laptop lid (game.js), replaced with an original "KM 0"
road-marker sticker.

No file in this repository is covered by a copyright carve-out — nothing here
is "for reference only", and everything may be redistributed. Most of it is
redistributable under the MIT License in LICENSE; the exceptions are the circuit
3D model in madring-3d/assets/madring-sketchfab/ and the two things derived from
it — images/madring-overhead.jpg and the MADRING centreline — which are
redistributable under CC-BY-4.0 with the credit set out in section 2, and the
four car sprites images/car-*.png, renders of the APEX FORMULA 2026 model
redistributable under Apache-2.0 as set out in section 2. Those are permissive
licences with attribution conditions, not restrictions on redistribution.


4. ADDED BY THIS PROJECT
------------------------

Original work by the Kilómetro Cero contributors, MIT licensed:

  - The four drivers — OSO, GATA, CIBELES and MADROÑO — including their
    portrait avatars, which are drawn from primitive shapes at runtime in
    BootScene.genDrivers() (game.js). Their car sprites are baked renders of
    the Apache-2.0 car model credited in section 2 (in the drivers' colours),
    with a procedural fallback drawn in the same genDrivers(). No third-party
    character art ships in either form.
  - The "KM 0" sticker described in section 3.
  - The `banking` terrain type, and the MADRING's dressing — the banked
    section, the tunnel spans, the nitro placement, the grid. The circuit's
    geometry is NOT ours and never was: the shape of the road is measured off
    the CC-BY-4.0 model credited in section 2, its position on the lap comes
    from the MIT-licensed geodata also credited there, and its scenery is a
    render of that same model. See scripts/MADRING-VALIDATION.md for exactly
    which number came from where.


